 const metadata={n:map.n,halfKpc:map.half,knownGridCells:known,catalogueExcludedCells:excluded,nonzeroCells:map.values.filter(v=>v>0).length,sourceBinNativePixels:64,layerSigmaKpc:.15,edgeFadePc:50,photoSpatialData:false,normalization:'Unit-integrated detected continuum-subtracted H-alpha surface morphology. One global luminosity in [0, 0.05] is fitted. Source pixels are divided by their angular area; no individual patch gain is fitted.',detection:'Median of 8×8 stratified native samples per 64-pixel bin; 3-sigma positive signal above the published zero. Noise is 1.4826 MAD of horizontal bin differences / sqrt(2). Spatial differences include real structure and continuum residuals: this is a conservative fluctuation proxy, not the survey photometric error. Negative residuals remain non-detections, not emission.',catalogueExclusion:'Any ray intersecting an existing finite gas primitive is excluded, including shell interiors. This conservative choice avoids counting its emission twice.',depth:'The map is placed on the unchanged warped plane and integrated with the adopted 150 pc Gaussian normal thickness. No depth is extruded along the Earth direction.',dereddening:'Conditional H-alpha correction exp(0.75 A_V / 1.085736), using OGLE red-clump internal A_V. This assumes the gas shares the tracer foreground column; gas tomography is unknown. The forward model then applies its unchanged native dust. Milky Way foreground is a common normalization here.',coverage:'Only three targeted source cutouts. Outside support is unknown and receives no new emission. A fixed 50 pc support fade prevents hard survey edges; it is a boundary prior, not a measurement.',source:'https://datalab.noirlab.edu/data/demcels',absoluteFluxClaim:false,inputs:inputs.map(s=>({id:s.id,pinMedian:s.pinMedian,pinDetectedSignal:s.pinSignal,noise:s.binned.noise,areaArcsec2:s.area,qualification:s.qualification}))};await writeFile(dir+'diffuse-gas.f32le',Buffer.from(map.values.buffer));await writeFile(dir+'dif